    "verilator": "5.029 devel"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The CLI is copied to an otherwise empty temporary directory and invoked with -I -S. Only Python standard-library imports are needed; no project Python, PyMTL, migration exporter, Git or source checkout is needed to run it.",
    "Nine unittest groups include many directed invalid inputs, isolated CLI execution, duplicate-key rejection, no overwrite, deterministic output, FU catalog IDs, memory variants, vector/FP constraints, graph ownership, memory ports and address-window permutations.",
    "Every frozen heterogeneous ARCH_* table declaration exactly matches the emitted packed value, width and ordering. The original manifest independently checks host, NoC and control widths.",
    "Five actual SV tops elaborate with generated bindings. A separate probe computes widths using native CGRA_PROFILE_PARAMETERS and $bits checks, independently of the tool formulas. These are elaboration checks with tied-off inputs, not program-functionality claims for all five examples.",
    "The actual 21-PE heterogeneous kernel uses the generated headers and bindings, completes all 21 PEs and verifies eight ordered final readbacks against independent arithmetic. Wrong-answer and permanent-stall negatives remain active.",
    "Shared memory attachment now rejects Context with StreamingMem and Streaming with ordinary Mem. Five positive catalogs include legal no-memory Context/Streaming. Existing Base rejection is preserved.",
    "The final emitter was rerun after correcting original-class aliases. Both generated SV files were byte-compared with the files used in all five compiled profiles and the kernel; the resulting final tool hash is recorded separately from the original build manifests.",
    "Compiler UNOPTFLAT diagnostics are recorded rather than suppressed or equated with verified graph SCCs. No emitted full-system netlist proof is claimed by this configuration-tool task; current-system SCC/synthesis refresh remains a later task.",
    "Program mapping, arbitrary coordinate remapping, sparse deleted tiles, general VC/credit counts and standalone single-PE configuration syntax are outside this architecture schema. Public cgra_pe SV parameterization is unchanged."
  ]
}
